cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "SynthesizerPlus: Synthetic Data Generation with Copulas, Evaluation and Multi-Format I/O"
abstract: >-
  An R package that generates synthetic versions of numeric, categorical,
  mixed-type and time-series data. Marginal distributions are modelled with
  interpolated empirical quantile functions and dependence with Gaussian or
  Student-t copulas; discrete and categorical variables enter through the
  distributional transform with maximum-likelihood (polychoric and polyserial)
  latent correlations, and missing values through missingness indicators in
  the copula. A closeness parameter, calibrated to a target distance or
  disclosure-risk level, controls how far the synthetic data move away from
  the real data. Fidelity, utility and disclosure risk are assessed with
  distributional distances, propensity-score mean squared error,
  confidence-interval overlap, correct attribution probability and distance
  to closest record. Data can be read from and written to CSV, Parquet,
  Feather, HDF5, JSON, Excel, SPSS, Stata, SAS and fst files.
